WEBVTT

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.150
<i>Portrait of Hell</i> .

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.820
The masterpiece from the middle
of Ryunosuke Akutagawa's career.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.650
Set in the medieval period,

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.780
its protagonist is a Kyoto
painter named Yoshihide.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.390
"Episode 7"

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.230
Yoshihide was the finest painter in the city,

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:07.900
but was shunned for his looks
and arrogant attitude.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:17.440
But he had one thing he loved
in his life: his daughter.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:25.150
One day, his noble patron orders him
to paint a portrait of hell.

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:29.070
Yoshihide can only paint things he's seen,

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:35.030
so he tortures his students in
an attempt to depict hell's torments.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:39.440
But the centerpiece of the painting,

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:45.150
the scene where a woman is to be burned
by the fires of hell, stymied him.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:49.650
A while later, Yoshihide is
summoned by his patron.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:55.150
He finds his daughter tied up inside a carriage.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:03:03.690
He does nothing to save his daughter
from the flames. He simply watches.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:10.650
Thus, the portrait of hell is completed,
and it is said to be a masterpiece.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:13.860
That sounds just like Ryu.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.150
Damn it!

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.190
Why can't I delve inside?

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:23.650
We've never had a situation
where no one could delve before.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:29.440
Normally, the tainted book would
call to someone, who could delve.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.110
If that's not happening...

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:36.530
Perhaps the book doesn't want
anyone to stop its destruction.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.730
Is that possible?

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:41.730
The protagonist of the story, Yoshihide,

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:47.030
reflects in a sense Ryu's ideals
about novels and art.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.230
Ideals?

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:53.820
An absolute devotion to art,
which separates art and life,

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:58.860
and is willing to sacrifice
everything to write. To create.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:03.110
That is the life he longed for.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:06.150
But he failed to realize it,

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:12.230
and denounced his old works
with a ferocity greater than anyone.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:20.940
Ryu once debated his friend Junichiro Tanizaki
in a series of magazine columns.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.070
"1927"

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.570
"Literary, All Too Literary"

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.610
There is one thought that is always
in my mind these days:

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:35.860
do novels really need dramatic stories?

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:42.570
Whether a story is truly "artistic"
is something I greatly doubt.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:45.230
Removing the interesting aspects of a story

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:49.530
means abandoning what makes novels unique.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:55.730
Don't readers look to novels to give
them a taste of the extraordinary?

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.820
And more than anything, Ryunosuke Akutagawa,

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:02.190
haven't your own books drawn more readers than

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:07.570
any others with the prospect
of fantastic stories?

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.650
Perhaps.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:13.030
But that's why I think...

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:18.360
...the words I wrote cannot form a true novel.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:22.820
And so the author denies his own novels?

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:27.230
Is that such a bad thing?

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:31.070
It's out of character for him.

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:35.820
For him to come to hate his own works later.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:40.360
I'm very curious to know what
caused such a change of heart.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.900
Hey! Dazai!

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.610
This has never happened before.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:54.650
A reincarnated author's book was tainted,
and its author swallowed up...

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:59.170
"Portrait of Hell"

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:59.570
Is the Taint just that strong?

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:00.780
Or...

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:05.730
Dazai?

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:07.030
What do you want?

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:10.650
No! Stop!

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.280
What are you doing?

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:17.860
What else?

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:20.690
I'm going to save Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:21.650
You can't!

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:24.820
The book has to call you before you can enter!

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:28.070
We won't know until we try!

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:32.030
Stop! Or it will taint you too!

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.150
You...

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:45.400
There's lots I want to say to Ryu too.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.780
I can't leave it to just you!

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:54.110
Listen to me for once, Ryu!

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:55.440
Both of you!

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.360
What?

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:15.400
Where are we?

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:22.110
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:24.030
You're both very stubborn.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:28.030
So please...

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.610
My book...

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.190
Where are we?

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:42.900
Inside the book, presumably.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.480
What a filthy man.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.150
I'd rather not look at him.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.900
Ryu!

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.900
He's always so gloomy.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:53.190
No, that's...

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:53.190
Who knows what thoughts are going through his head...

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:54.730
I see.

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:58.940
He's turned into Yoshihide,
the protagonist of the book?

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:01.900
Father!

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:06.190
Oh, you came to get me?

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:07.150
Yes.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:09.650
Dinner's ready.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.280
What do we do?

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:22.150
If we lead this book to its proper conclusion,
we can save the book.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.530
So I'm going to...

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:29.070
Well, let's see what you can do, I guess.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.570
Excuse me!

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:36.730
Coming!

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:39.820
Hello.

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:42.940
I'm a traveling painter of no renown.

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:48.780
Yoshihide- <i>san</i> , I've heard of
your skill and have a request.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:52.190
--Please make me your student.
--I refuse.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:54.400
I'm not interested.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.610
Please leave.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.690
Come on! Please!

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:01.480
I'm a big fan! I'm begging you!

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:03.780
I'll do your chores and stuff!

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:04.480
No.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.650
Please! Please!

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.650
Dad, he seems to really want it.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:08.860
Why not make him your student?

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:12.650
Way to go, daughter! You're smart! And pretty!

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.650
If you say so...

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:13.940
Hooray!

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:17.860
Great, huh?

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:19.230
Thank you.

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:21.730
It's thanks to you...

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:25.530
I don't know when the Taint
will try to interfere.

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:30.440
So the safest thing to do
should be to stay by his side.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.360
He lives with his daughter?

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:41.480
Sensei...

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:44.480
Do we have to climb up this high?

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:46.730
That looks like a good spot!

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.980
We're going all the way up there?

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:52.030
I was told to paint birds flying in the sky.

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:54.980
So you came all the way up here?

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:58.070
I can only paint what I see.

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:03.860
Only after seeing it can I make it my own.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:08.900
And only then can I turn the image
in my mind into a picture.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.820
Make it your own?

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:14.150
It's the only way I know to paint.

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:15.820
This makes no sense...

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:45.900
It's not supposed to be such a peaceful story!

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:49.650
Is the story's development being stopped?

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.530
If that's possible...

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:08.320
I knew you'd be there, Taint!

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:18.900
Wait!

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.360
Intruder! Get him!

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:23.610
Where is he?

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:25.400
Don't lose him!

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:26.530
Follow him!

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:32.110
Who is it this time?

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:34.440
I already have a student.

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:36.570
You seem happy.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:38.980
Where'd he go?

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:41.440
Work's going well.

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:44.650
Your daughter is all smiles.

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:49.980
Nothing dramatic happens, but it's a good life.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.780
What are you trying to say?

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:54.440
A peaceful life with no story.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:59.440
Maybe this is what you really wanted to write.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.480
Huh?

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.110
Tell me, Ryu.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:06.030
If you regret writing this story...

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:08.860
What?

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:18.030
You!

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.440
That hurts. What's wrong with you?

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:26.280
I knew something was off!

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:31.530
Why did you delve when you hated
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> 's books?

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.610
I don't hate them. I criticized them.

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:36.570
You intend to erase them, don't you?

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:40.110
Erase his books because you don't like them!

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:48.030
In his last years, Ryu hated his past works
and their emphasis on stories.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.480
But that doesn't mean...

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:51.820
This <i>Portrait of Hell</i> is like a curse

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:56.610
that Ryu created to devour himself.

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:59.820
Are you really Shiga?

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:02.570
Or did a Taint take you over?

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:08.440
I can't let you get near Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:10.320
I'll protect this book!

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.320
Do whatever you want.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.110
Wait!

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.400
Father!

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:31.730
Our lord wants your daughter.

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:33.110
Feel honored.

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:34.320
Father!

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:36.940
Wait! Don't take her!

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:38.230
Father!

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:42.190
Yes. This is what should happen.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:43.530
What's wrong?

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:45.440
Get closer to me.

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.360
Is there something you want?

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:51.190
I'll give you anything you want.

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:54.150
I want nothing.

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:55.110
A folding screen?

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.320
Yes.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:14:00.900
It seems your daughter misses her father deeply.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:04.480
I thought that perhaps she
would feel less lonely if

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:08.320
she had something her father painted.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:11.230
What sort of painting would you like?

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:15.110
Hmm... Hell.

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:17.320
I want hell.

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:20.280
Hell?

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:26.690
Yes. Paint me a scene of misery
and terror from the depths of hell.

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:28.820
You're the finest painter in Kyoto.

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:32.480
You can do it easily, right?

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:35.110
So you're going to paint it for him?

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:36.900
Yes, I will.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:40.650
If I make him something of incredible quality,

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:44.900
perhaps he'll give her back.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.570
I'm going to do it.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:48.780
Sensei...

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:51.650
And I need your help.

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:53.280
Come with me.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.820
Huh?

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:56.030
Why?!

00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:57.570
I told you.

00:14:57.570 --> 00:15:00.030
I can only paint what I've seen.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:06.570
The folding screen needs a painting
of a sinner being tied up by hell's demons.

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:08.570
I know that, but...

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:11.780
I want more of an expression of pure suffering!

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:13.980
It's digging in! It's digging in!

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:17.690
Is this necessary?

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:19.440
Is this really necessary?

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:22.110
I want more suffering!

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:26.900
Damn it!

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:34.280
Come closer.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:37.980
I told you, I'll give you anything you want.

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:40.190
What upsets you?

00:15:40.190 --> 00:15:42.730
What do you want?

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:46.820
I want to return to my father.

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:54.030
Lord!

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:56.030
The painter...

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:57.070
What?

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:00.320
You can't paint it?

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:02.820
What do you mean you can't paint it?

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:08.570
I want to paint a girl being burned
by hellfire in the center of the screen.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:13.440
But I can only paint what I've seen.

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:16.150
That's not an excuse.

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:18.230
I can't do it, and that's the end of it.

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:27.900
But you could if you saw it, right?

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:29.690
Yes. But...

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:31.570
Very well.

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:36.110
I'll help you, then.

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:38.730
Th-This is...

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:41.650
Be thankful, painter.

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:47.570
I'll show you a scene from hell.

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:48.780
Father!

00:16:57.730 --> 00:17:00.480
Father! Father!

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:02.820
Help me, Father!

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:09.110
Father!

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:10.070
Wait!

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:11.650
Where are you going?

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:17.480
You... What are you doing?

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:19.900
Go back, Sensei.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:21.530
This isn't right.

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:23.570
What are you talking about?

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:26.440
What kind of father would let his daughter burn?

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:29.780
But this story...

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:31.280
Thank you, Father.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:32.860
For saving me.

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:35.030
I love you...

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.780
A gentle father who saves his daughter.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:41.780
What's wrong with that? What's bad about that?

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:44.980
It's this story that's wrong.

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:48.190
It should disappear.

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:50.860
There you are...

00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:53.690
What is this?

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:56.730
Get back, Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> .

00:17:56.730 --> 00:17:58.190
Akutagawa?

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:14.230
You're going to burn and die,
and never even be painted.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:17.320
Too bad, delver.

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:31.730
I was a little worried,

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:33.730
but it seems to have cut you just fine.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:40.690
You...

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:42.530
You screwed up big, kid.

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:44.480
If you knew, you should've helped!

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:46.030
Yeah, right.

00:18:46.030 --> 00:18:51.030
No way in hell you were going
to listen to a word I said.

00:18:51.030 --> 00:18:53.820
We didn't finish our discussion, Ryu.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:59.280
If you regret writing this book,
I'm fine with that.

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:03.690
After you finish a book,
you think you're the greatest writer ever.

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:07.070
And then the next day is filled
with drinking and regrets.

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:15.900
And on the third day, you love it even more.

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:21.070
I criticized your books, Ryu.

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:25.190
But I've never wanted them to disappear.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:40.690
Ryu, even if <i>Portrait of Hell</i> is,
to you, a curse,

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:45.480
it's still a part of your soul.

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:49.980
So...

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:08.900
Don't let your guard down!

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:13.110
It's hopeless.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:20.110
If the girl gets away, the story is...

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.360
I won't let that happen!

00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:28.230
Ryu!

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:32.150
Look closely!

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:22.460
"Portrait of Hell"

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:37.190
Thank you, Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:42.940
No, it wasn't me who saved your book.

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:44.570
It was Shiga.

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:57.860
"Portrait of Hell"

00:23:28.320 --> 00:23:29.730
Literary Gourmet!

00:23:29.730 --> 00:23:32.690
"Forget about <i>Katsu</i> Sandwiches
and Think of Girls."

00:23:32.690 --> 00:23:35.530
You like sandwiches, right, Tanizaki- <i>kun</i> ?

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:40.020
" <i>Katsu</i> Sandwich: A filling meal of crispy <i>katsu</i> and
plenty of shredded cabbage between toasted bread."

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:38.440
The combination of <i>katsu</i> sandwiches and coffee is delicious.

00:23:38.440 --> 00:23:40.690
And there're other things I recommend too.

00:23:41.360 --> 00:23:42.150
What's that?

00:23:42.150 --> 00:23:44.780
A sandwich of sausages and cucumbers...

00:23:44.780 --> 00:23:47.190
I find it so tantalizing...

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:48.480
Why high heels?

00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:51.280
This feels like we can't broadcast it...

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:54.150
Look at this ripe, juicy cucumber...

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:54.150
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> , let's call off the broadcast!

00:23:54.150 --> 00:23:56.320
Like the curves of a beautiful woman...

00:23:54.150 --> 00:23:58.230
Stop! Stop! Stop!

00:23:56.320 --> 00:23:58.230
I can't take it anymore!

00:23:58.230 --> 00:23:59.780
No more!
